{"version":1,"summary":"Requires Go 1.27.3 so govulncheck no longer reports GO-2026-6809, and stops concurrent test children from racing on one coverage directory.","files":[{"path":"go.mod","summary":"Raises the go directive to 1.27.3.","annotations":[{"newRange":[3,3],"summary":"The go directive moves from 1.27.2 to 1.27.3, the release that fixes GO-2026-6809.","rationale":"Go 1.27.2 ships a vulnerable crypto/x509, so the vuln check is red on main. CI reads go-version-file: go.mod, so this line selects the fixed toolchain. Verified with scripts/ci on Go 1.27.3 and the GitHub vuln check.","author":"fm/verilex-go-1273"}]},{"path":"tests/run_test.go","summary":"Gives each spawned CLI its own GOCOVERDIR subdirectory.","annotations":[{"newRange":[131,139],"summary":"command() points every child at a unique child-N coverage subdirectory under GOCOVERDIR.","rationale":"Six children exiting together wrote the same covmeta temp file name on macOS, because the name repeats within a clock tick, so one rename failed and TestKeptInstanceGoesToExactlyOneContinuingRun saw exit 2. Separate directories remove the shared name. Verified by scripts/ci locally on Linux; the race itself only shows on macOS CI.","author":"fm/verilex-go-1273"}]},{"path":"scripts/ci","summary":"Reads coverage from all child subdirectories.","annotations":[{"newRange":[57,57],"summary":"covdata percent now receives every directory under the cover root, joined by commas.","rationale":"covdata does not recurse, so without this the subdirectories would report no coverage.","author":"fm/verilex-go-1273"}]}]}
